      "repair_reason": "- [P1] Maintainers need to choose one canonical candidate and require exact real-behavior proof; automation cannot supply the contributor's runtime proof or decide between overlapping PRs.; Cleared: The diff only changes TypeScript error-message branching and focused tests; it does not add dependencies, workflows, permissions, network calls, secrets handling, or package execution paths. (sha=cbb7acc553b4394d0871b7378cd3ea23ccf39dda)",
      "review_summary": "Adds an `openai-codex`-specific missing-model hint in embedded-agent model resolution and regression tests for legacy, built-in, and custom provider hint behavior.\n\nPR surface: Source +8, Tests +42. Total +50 across 2 files.\n\nReproducibility: yes. source-level: current main still falls through to the generic `models.providers[...]` hint for unresolved configured `openai-codex` model refs, and current validation rejects the reported `models.providers.openai-codex` overlay without `baseUrl`. I did not run a live Docker crash-loop reproduction in this read-only review.",
